  "summary": "Ulm Minster is a Gothic parish church in Ulm, Germany, paid for by the town's citizens. Its foundation stone was laid on 30 June 1377, building stopped in 1543, and work on the main steeple finished in 1890, when the tower stood 161.53 m high according to the City of Ulm.",
